# .graphifyignore - data/config JSON that graphify's extractor accepts but which
# carries no code symbols.
#
# Why this file exists: graphify registers a JSON extractor for every .json, but
# only emits nodes for manifest-shaped ones (package.json, tsconfig*.json,
# manifest.json, railway.json, components.json, turbo.json). Everything else
# lands in the #1666 "produced zero nodes and are absent from the graph" warning
# on every single run - 131 files as of 2026-07-30. That warning exists to
# surface files `affected`/`explain` are blind through, so a permanent 131-file
# list trains you to skim the one signal that would matter the day a real .ts
# goes empty. Excluding the known-inert data files makes it meaningful again.
#
# Nothing here is lost from the graph: these files already produced zero nodes.
#
# Syntax is gitignore (merged with .gitignore, last-match-wins). Note that this
# file can only ever EXCLUDE more - a `!` negation cannot pull back a file that
# .gitignore already dropped.
#
# TIGHT PATTERNS ONLY. Several of these directories also hold JSON that DOES
# produce nodes, so directory-wide globs would silently shrink the graph:
#   - last30days-skill/mcp/manifest.json          (glob on last30days-skill/**)
#   - apps/nickstire/client/public/manifest.json  (glob on client/public/*)
#   - reports/security-audit.json                 (glob on reports/*)
#   - **/vendor/bird-search/package.json          (sits one level above lib/)
# Never ignore tsconfig*.json: graphify reads it for TypeScript path-alias
# resolution (extract.py:196), so dropping it would degrade import edges
# repo-wide, not just remove nodes.

# --- Drizzle migration snapshots (generated schema state, not code) ---
apps/nickstire/drizzle/meta/*.json

